<decision #track.add-ai-workflow-profile-source-loaders.authority apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEV>
  AI workflow hosts should parse profile roots themselves or consume depa-flows loaders?
  </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEV>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEW>
    Consume depa-flows loaders.
    </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEW>
    <decision-text ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEX>
    Profile root parsing, substrate lowering and diagnostics are canonical depa-flows responsibilities.
    </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEX>
    <rationale ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEY>
    This prevents parallel workflow semantics in every host integration.
    </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEY>
    <evidence ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEZ>
    Existing public XNL examples use AI profile roots while substrate loaders reject those roots.
    </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPEZ>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.add-ai-workflow-profile-source-loaders.compatibility apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF0>
  Should existing substrate loaders silently accept AI profile roots?
  </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF0>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF1>
    No.
    </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF1>
    <decision-text ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF2>
    Add explicit profile-root loader primitives and AI facades; keep existing substrate root acceptance unchanged.
    </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF2>
    <rationale ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF3>
    Explicit APIs preserve product identity and avoid turning current names into ambiguous aliases.
    </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF3>
    <evidence ?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF4>
    Canonical product naming behavior and no-legacy-alias policy.
    </?01M0NJZ4SYRC12RXH68C6VKPF4>
  )>
)>
